# Android Studio writes local.properties itself on first open. It points at
# your own SDK install and is machine-specific, so it is not committed.
sdk.dir=/Users/<you>/Library/Android/sdk

# Dengage REST API user, from Settings > API User in the panel. These let the
# Test Area send this device a real push through the transactional API.
#
# They are read here rather than committed because THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC.
# The credentials are account-wide across account 28, contact data included, so
# publishing them is not the same risk as shipping them inside an internal APK.
# Fill these in and every APK you build is demo-ready; leave them out and the
# Test Area falls back to firing its event and says so on screen.
#
# Use a DEDICATED API user with the narrowest role that can send a
# transactional push, never an administrator, so a leak costs one rotation.
dengage.api.userkey=<your API user>
dengage.api.password=<its password>
